  "aero": {
    "_note": "Aero forces are ½ ρ C A v² with the car's velocity through the air (minus wind, m/s world frame) and ρ from the standard atmosphere at the car's altitude (the world gives its ground level's altitude). Drag (dragCoefficient × frontalArea) acts at the centre of mass along the airflow. front / rear.liftCoefficient (+ lift, − downforce, also × frontalArea) act at their points (car frame, m), so the balance changes the handling: this car makes a little lift at both ends, so it gets lighter at speed. Air hitting the body from the side (sliding) raises drag up to sideways.dragFactor × and loses sideways.liftLoss of the lift / downforce, both by sin² of the angle. Parts (parts/*.json) add their own coefficients at their sockets. These are the bare shell's: the body parts add their share (aeroEffect), so a car with every stock panel on has drag 0.38, front lift 0.08 and rear lift 0.1.",
