  "wheels": {
    "_note": "Which corners make up each axle, and the suspension's top mounts: mountHeight m above the model's wheel sockets (the wheels' centres at ride height). The stock suspension settles to exactly this length under the stock car's weight, so the stock car sits on its sockets; stiffer, shorter or softer suspension (or more weight) sits it higher or lower. The wheels themselves are the fitted rims and tyres: each corner's radius is its rim plus the tyre's sidewall (to the mm), its turning inertia hubInertia (the hub, brake disc and drive shaft) plus the rim's and tyre's from their mass and size; referenceOffset is the rim offset the model's sockets are for (less offset, or spacers, puts a wheel further out); unsprungBaseline is the wheel and tyre mass per corner the suspension was set up with (a heavier wheel puts the difference straight onto its tyre).",
