  "assists": {
    "_note": "Driver aids: each can be switched on and off in the game's settings (these are the defaults). ABS: per wheel, when the slip passes releaseAt × the tyre's peak-grip slip it dumps pressure at releaseRate (share per second, down to minPressure), holds holdTime s once the slip is back under reapplyAt × peak, then reapplies at applyRate — it pulses; off below minSpeed m/s. Traction control closes the throttle once a driven wheel slips past its target (fully by a window later): straightSlipTarget / Window pointing straight, easing to slipTarget / slipWindow as you steer or drift; strength 0..1 (0.5 = these values, 1 = half, 0 = double). The slide limiter (with traction control) fades the drive once the rear slides past angle rad (looking lookAhead s ahead). Stability control: expected yaw rate = speed × tan(front angle) ÷ (wheelbase × (1 + (speed / characteristicSpeed)²)), capped by grip; turning faster than that by yawThreshold rad/s with the rear sliding past slipAllowance rad (driftSlipAllowance with the drift assist on), or by strongYawError, brakes the outside front (oversteerGain N·m per rad/s); turning slower brakes the inside rear (understeerGain) and the inside front by understeerFrontShare of that; at most maxTorque, easing the throttle by up to throttleCut; above minSpeed m/s; it leaves oversteer alone while the handbrake is held and handbrakeHold s after. Rev protection (off by default) refuses a downshift that would put the engine past its redline (or the gearbox's maxDownshiftRpm, if lower); without it any downshift goes in, and one at too high a speed over-revs the engine (engine.overRev). Countersteer, steering and drift assists are for keyboard / gamepad (see steering.counterSteer and the drift section).",
